# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored — REAL secrets go there, NOT here.
# This file is the template — anything committed here is public the moment you push to git.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Site
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The canonical URL of the live site. Drives metadataBase, sitemap, robots, canonical links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://bricknclick.com

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contact form (Gmail SMTP via Nodemailer)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# We send contact-form submissions via the brand Gmail account using SMTP.
# Free, no third-party dependency, works immediately.
#
# One-time setup:
#   1. Sign in to the Gmail account you want to use (e.g. bricknclick.ai@gmail.com)
#   2. Enable 2-Step Verification: https://myaccount.google.com/security
#   3. Generate an App Password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#      → App: "Mail"  → Device: "Other" → name it "Bricknclick form"
#   4. Copy the 16-character password (Google shows it once — you can't view it again)
#   5. Paste below into your .env.local
#
# NOTE: The App Password is NOT your normal Gmail password. Don't use that.
GMAIL_USER=your-account@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Where contact-form submissions get delivered.
# Defaults to GMAIL_USER (i.e. they land in the same inbox you're sending from).
# Override only if you want them routed elsewhere (e.g. an info@bricknclick.com
# alias that forwards into a different team mailbox).
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=info@bricknclick.com

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Sheets backup (optional)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# If set, every form submission ALSO writes a row to a Google Sheet via a
# free Google Apps Script Web App webhook. Email + Sheet fire in parallel,
# so the lead is captured even if one channel fails.
#
# Setup (one-time, ~5 min):
#   1. Create a new Google Sheet (call it "Bricknclick leads")
#   2. Extensions → Apps Script → paste the script (see project docs / route comments)
#   3. Deploy → New deployment → Web app
#      Execute as:  Me
#      Who has access:  Anyone
#   4. Authorize → copy the Web App URL it gives you
#   5. Paste below
#
# Leave commented out / unset to skip the sheet backup entirely — route works fine
# with email-only.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycb.../exec
